<article class="env-lemma" id="04DF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04DF">Lemma <span data-tag="04DF">29.46.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is a universal homeomorphism, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is integral, universally injective and surjective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $f$ is a universal homeomorphism. By Lemma <a href="/tag/04DE" data-tag="04DE">29.46.4</a> we see that $f$ is affine. Since $f$ is clearly universally closed we see that $f$ is integral by Lemma <a href="/tag/01WM" data-tag="01WM">29.45.7</a>. It is also clear that $f$ is universally injective and surjective. 
    <p>
      Assume $f$ is integral, universally injective and surjective. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01WM" data-tag="01WM">29.45.7</a> $f$ is universally closed. Since it is also universally bijective (see Lemma <a href="/tag/01S1" data-tag="01S1">29.9.4</a>) we see that it is a universal homeomorphism. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>